label chapter_3_2:
    scene bg JP RESTAURANT

    nvl hide dissolve

    som "\"Yes, she's a very respectable girl. She worked day and night to get those awards!\""

    shf "\"I wish my daughter could be more like yours!\""

    shf "\"They're friends, so why don't they teach other Mathematics? Sofia's always been better at it than her. It's a shame, because it's Shasha's lowest grade...\""

    som "\"How about it, Sofia? Maybe Shasha's father could even pay you to be her tutor!\""

    no "My mother erupts into laughter. Sharlene's father laughs with the joke, but it somehow feels like it doesn't reach his eyes. I stared directly at the sea creatures in front of me. Dead salmon, dead tuna, dead eel, dead urchin. Sharlene. She looked ashamed to even be sitting there. She hasn't taken a single piece of food either. I found it annoying that they chose to talk to me, and I wished that the sea creature in front of me would also drop dead."

    no "Sharlene always looks so easy to tease. It might be the only source of entertainment I have these days."

    so "\"I'd be glad to help her. She might even need to learn more than just math from me.\""

    so "\"Sh... Sharlene's never been the bright type, after all. But that's not inherently her fault.\""

    no "Sharlene's eyes didn't reflect the light―in fact, they never did even in other places. That's because she always has her head at this awkward angle, looking down while trying to squint up. Someone taught her that eye contact was important and she always makes a point to remind me. Her eyes are squinting away."

    sh "\"But Sofia wastes her time playing games with me...\""

    som "\"You―you're not lying about my child again, are you?\""

    no "Sharlene's face contorted in a way I haven't seen in a while. It was one of her funnier displays."

    sh "\"I wouldn't lie! Especially not to her mom!\""

    sh "\"W―Why would I do that? She's really good at Pomorimo Online!\""

    som "\"Pomo... dear, what is she talking about...?\""

    so "\"It's a pomodoro timer thing. For work habits?\""

    sh "\"You―\""

    no "I saw Sharlene doing that habit where she'd chew on the inside of her mouth. It always made her look like a bloated fish of sorts. She sinks away from the conversation and springs up abruptly from her seat. None of the adults react. They're used to her stupid outbursts."

    no "I was starting to feel even sicker from the smell invading my nostrils, and my legs stood up before I could explain to my mother what I was doing. Now I needed to act like I had some compassion."

    so "\"I'm just checking on her. Okay, mama?\""

    som "\"That'd be good, yes. You manage to still be so kind even when she's so troublesome, Sofia.\""

    so "\"... Hahaha.\""

    so "\"Of course.\""

    return
